# {{.Name}}

A scheduled Sora JavaScript worker. Uses the same permission-checked
`window.soraExt.call` methods as panels and `console.log` for its extension
log. The source uses real extension settings and the current session state.

Workers run in fresh goja processes while the app is open (including hidden
in the tray). Effective interval: 15 minutes to 7 days. Per-run budgets:
2 CPU seconds, 128 MiB committed process memory, 30 seconds wall time.
No filesystem, process, raw socket, DOM, module loader or timers.
`onEvent` gives a session snapshot once per subscription per run.

For network requests, explicitly add the net.fetch permission and
network_hosts allowlist, then use:

```js
const response = await window.soraExt.call('net.fetch', {url: 'https://api.example.com/status'});
console.log('HTTP ' + response.status);
```

Replace the example host with your actual endpoint. Fetch is HTTPS-only,
allowlisted, and uses the VPN proxy or fails closed. Disable, uninstall or
closing the app stops the worker. Failures produce a notification and log.

## Build and sign

```sh
sora-ext validate
sora-ext pack . -o /tmp/{{.ID}}.soraext
sora-ext sign --key .sora/author.key /tmp/{{.ID}}.soraext
```

Keep .sora/author.key private and offline; never put it in a package or Git.
See docs/extensions.md for the full runtime and security contract.
